# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository, regardless of what
# line endings a given checkout/editor/OS writes on disk. This repo has
# repeatedly picked up CRLF corruption across many files at once (whole
# working-tree diffs where every insertion is matched by an identical
# deletion — a line-ending flip, not a real content change), most
# recently ~212 files after a routine branch checkout. That's costly to
# diagnose and risks a real edit getting lost in the noise. `text=auto`
# lets git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` pins the normalized form to
# LF on checkout so every clone/checkout converges on the same bytes
# instead of drifting per-environment.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by line-ending normalization regardless
# of extension-based auto-detection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
